AgentCore Identity – OAuth2 Credential Provider Validation (Auth0)
Objective

Validate that AgentCore Identity can securely obtain an OAuth2 access token from an external Identity Provider (Auth0) on behalf of a registered workload using a configured OAuth2 Credential Provider.

What Was Tested

We tested the outbound OAuth2 token exchange flow from AgentCore Identity to Auth0 using the Client Credentials grant.

This test focused specifically on validating:

Workload identity authentication within AgentCore

OAuth2 Credential Provider configuration

Token exchange via external IdP (Auth0)

Successful issuance of a scoped JWT access token

This was an identity plumbing validation, not an API authorization test.

Step-by-Step Flow Validated
1. Workload Identity Validation

Confirmed the workload is registered in AgentCore Identity.

Successfully called:

get_workload_access_token(workload_name=...)

Received a valid workloadAccessToken.

Result:
AgentCore recognizes and authenticates the workload.

2. OAuth2 Credential Provider Configuration

Created (or confirmed existing) OAuth2 Credential Provider in AgentCore Identity.

Configured with:

Auth0 discovery URL (/.well-known/openid-configuration)

Client ID

Client Secret

Token endpoint

Confirmed provider exists and is reusable.

Result:
AgentCore can securely store and use OAuth client credentials.

3. Token Exchange (Core Validation)

Used the workload access token to initiate OAuth token exchange via the credential provider.

Requested:

auth_flow = "M2M"

scopes = ["read:test"]

audience = https://agent-core-test-api

Flow executed:

Workload
   ↓
AgentCore Identity
   ↓
OAuth2 Credential Provider
   ↓
Auth0 /oauth/token (client_credentials)
   ↓
JWT Access Token Returned

Result:
AgentCore successfully obtained a JWT access token from Auth0.

4. JWT Validation

Decoded the returned token and verified:

iss → Auth0 tenant URL

aud → https://agent-core-test-api

scope → read:test

gty → client-credentials

Valid expiration timestamps

Result:
Auth0 issued a properly scoped access token for the configured API.

What This Test Proved

AgentCore Identity can act as an OAuth2 token broker.

Workloads can securely obtain scoped third-party access tokens.

OAuth client credentials are centralized in the credential provider (not embedded in application code).

External IdP integration (Auth0) works end-to-end.

Client Credentials (Machine-to-Machine) flow is fully functional.

What This Test Did NOT Cover

This test did not validate:

Backend API token enforcement

API Gateway / Lambda authorizers

IAM role assumption

Inbound user authentication

Resource-level authorization checks

This was strictly an outbound OAuth token minting validation.

Architectural Significance

This enables the following enterprise use cases:

Calling external APIs protected by Auth0

Integrating AgentCore workloads with enterprise IdPs (Auth0 / Okta)

Enforcing workload-level identity boundaries

Centralized OAuth provider management

Eliminating direct secret handling in runtime code

One-Line Executive Summary

Validated that AgentCore Identity can exchange a workload identity for a scoped Auth0 JWT access token using an OAuth2 credential provider via the client credentials flow.
